  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `chord_clears` moved from `slots.rs` to the new `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chord_clear.rs` (`slots.rs` re-exports it).\n- The law splits the chord at each loop vertex that the chord touches without a crossing. The midpoint of each piece must be in the closed region. Before, one midpoint decided the full chord.\n\n## The cause\n\nThe part pinches the band between the part and the stock. Thus, the cutter-centre area has pieces whose walls are on one line (Y -32, the offset edge of the stock). The old law found no edge that crossed the chord from (-8.05, -32) to (32, -32), and it read one midpoint, which was in a piece. Thus, the 2D Adaptive path fed along Y -32 at each level, 0.94 mm into the part.\n\nThe issue gives \"10 mm at (-1.44, -29.94)\". That value comes from the stock in the first report: its top is at Z 10, and the top of the part is at Z 20. The sim reads each part column above the stock as a 10 mm gouge, and (-1.44, -29.94) is the first part column. The pin uses a stock that covers the part.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/adaptive_pinch.rs`:\n  - `a_whole_model_clearing_never_joins_two_corners_across_the_part_that_pinches_them`: a 20 mm disc in a 31 mm stock. 2D Adaptive and 2D Offset, aligned and turned stock. The cutter stays off the disc, and the op has no warnings.\n  - `the_users_part_with_default_adaptive_keeps_the_cutter_off_it` (heavy lane, about 5 min in debug): `Milling-test.step` in a 70 x 70 x 27 box on Z -7, 2D Adaptive seed params, through `GenerateOperation` (`operation::generate`). Aligned and turned stock: the cutter reaches less than 0.06 mm into the part section at each Z, and the op has 0 warnings. Aligned stock: `simulate_document` has 0 gouge cells.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chord_clear.rs`: two unit tests (a chord across the gap between two pieces does not clear; a graze along one wall clears).\n- Mutation: with the old midpoint law, all three pins fail (\"reaches 0.936 into the part\" at (1.963, -32.000, 15.000); \"0.479 into the disc\"; the gap chord clears). A first draft also split the chord at the ends of collinear edges. With that branch removed, all pins pass, so I removed it (the vertex split does that work).\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (motion suites 145 s, app suites 209 s, 0 failed). It includes `golden_cl` and `solid_law_goldens`. No golden moved.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The pin uses an end mill with 30 mm flutes. With the catalog's 15 mm flutes, the 25 mm deep part gives `ShankHit` warnings at the lower levels. That refusal is correct and is not part of this issue.\n- The sim pin runs only on the aligned stock. The program sim does not run on the turned stock; the op check covers it.\n- The keep law of #1615 is not on main, so this PR does not run it.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1620-chord-pieces.md`.\n\nThe branch is based on c00ba18a and merges upstream/main 3ead1295.\n\nChangelog: A 2D clearing no longer feeds across the part between two pieces of the cutter area whose walls are on one line (whole-model 2D Adaptive on Milling-test.step cut 0.94 mm into the part).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1620\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
